The evidence is consistent: all user-visible errors fall in the first two minutes, and the refused connection is the only failure mode on the route-plan → travel2 path. I'm confident enough to write the answer.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-travel2-service",
      "fault_kind": "network_partition",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT cl.service_name, cl.attr_http_response_status_code code, count(*) n, sum(CASE WHEN s.span_id IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) no_child_span FROM abnormal_traces cl LEFT JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id=cl.span_id WHERE cl.service_name='ts-route-plan-service' AND cl.attr_span_kind='Client' AND cl.attr_status_code='Error' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "All 64 failing route-plan Client calls returned 503 and have no child server span, so the request never reached a server."},
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, substr(message,1,300) m, count(*) n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='ts-route-plan-service' AND message LIKE '%Connection refused%' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Route-plan logs 64 SEVERE 503 errors: upstream connect error, transport failure 'Connection refused'."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT CAST(floor(epoch(time)/60) AS BIGINT) m, sum(CASE WHEN service_name='ts-route-plan-service' AND attr_span_kind='Client' AND attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) refused, sum(CASE WHEN service_name='ts-route-plan-service' AND span_name='RoutePlanController.getMinStopStations' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) mss_calls, sum(CASE WHEN service_name='ts-travel2-service' AND span_name LIKE '%trips/routes%' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) travel2_routes_srv FROM abnormal_traces GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1", "claim": "Refusals occur only in the first two minutes of the window; afterwards every route-plan to travel2 call succeeds."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT p.attr_status_code ist, c.attr_status_code cst, c.attr_http_response_status_code ccode, cs.service_name child_svc, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces p JOIN abnormal_traces c ON c.parent_span_id=p.span_id LEFT JOIN abnormal_traces cs ON cs.parent_span_id=c.span_id WHERE p.service_name='ts-route-plan-service' AND p.span_name='RoutePlanController.getMinStopStations' GROUP BY 1,2,3,4 ORDER BY 5 DESC", "claim": "Failed getMinStopStations executions lose the third downstream call, the travel2 trips/routes call, which is replaced by a childless 503."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "ts-travel2-service", "to": "ts-route-plan-service", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT c.service_name callee, c.span_name, c.attr_status_code, c.attr_http_response_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces p ON c.parent_span_id=p.span_id WHERE p.service_name='ts-route-plan-service' AND c.service_name='ts-route-plan-service' AND c.attr_span_kind='Server' AND c.attr_status_code='Error' GROUP BY 1,2,3,4", "claim": "Route-plan's minStopStations server spans return 500 in 64 traces where the travel2 call was refused."}]},
    {"from": "ts-route-plan-service", "to": "ts-travel-plan-service", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_http_response_status_code code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND attr_http_response_status_code=500 GROUP BY 1,2,3,4", "claim": "Travel-plan's minStation server spans return 500 after calling route-plan's failing minStopStations endpoint."}]},
    {"from": "ts-travel-plan-service", "to": "ts-ui-dashboard", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_http_response_status_code code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND attr_http_response_status_code=503 GROUP BY 1,2,3,4", "claim": "ui-dashboard returns 503 to users in the same window, the user-facing error from the travel-plan failure."}]}
